; My ledger
;
; The top of your ledger: Beancount and Fava start reading here.
; It is plain text and yours to edit, in Beanbook or on a computer. Beanbook
; never rewrites parts of it you did not change. Lines that start with a
; semicolon are comments, and Beancount ignores them.

option "title" "My ledger"

;; Currencies
; The first operating currency is the one totals and the dashboard use.
; Add another operating_currency line to see reports in that currency too.
option "operating_currency" "EUR"

; How a sale chooses which purchase it comes from. STRICT asks you whenever it
; is not clear. Others: FIFO, LIFO, HIFO, STRICT_WITH_SIZE. One account can
; differ: put the method after its currency in its open line.
option "booking_method" "STRICT"

;; Precision
; How far apart the two sides of an entry may be and still balance, when the
; amounts do not say (an amount written as 12, with no decimals).
; https://beancount.github.io/docs/precision_tolerances.html
option "inferred_tolerance_default" "EUR:0.005"

; How many decimal places figures are shown with.
option "display_precision" "EUR:0.01"

;; Documents
; Receipts and statements are kept in this folder, one folder per account.
option "documents" "documents"

;; Plugins
; Plugins check or add to entries as the ledger loads. Their order matters.

; Opens the receipt named in an entry's document: line. Part of Fava.
plugin "fava.plugins.link_documents"

; More checks. Remove the semicolon at the start of a line to turn one on.
; Every currency needs a commodity line in files/commodities.beancount:
; plugin "beancount.plugins.check_commodity"
; Post only to the last level of an account, Expenses:Food:Groceries and not Expenses:Food:
; plugin "beancount.plugins.leafonly"
; Two different prices for one commodity on the same day are an error:
; plugin "beancount.plugins.unique_prices"
; A sale at a price must post its gain or loss to an Income account:
; plugin "beancount.plugins.sellgains"
; Every opened account must be used. Turn on once your accounts are in use:
; plugin "beancount.plugins.nounused"

;; Fava
; Settings for the reports. Fava reads them from these dated lines; the date
; means nothing else.
2026-09-30 custom "fava-option" "default-file" "files/transactions.beancount"
; The day your financial year ends, as month-day. 12-31 when left out.
; 2026-09-30 custom "fava-option" "fiscal-year-end" "06-30"

;; Files
include "files/commodities.beancount"
include "files/accounts.beancount"
include "prices/prices.beancount"
include "files/transactions.beancount"
